{{relevant tutorial|Turtle farming}}
'''Turtles''' are [[passive mobs]] found in [[beach]] biomes. They can be bred with [[seagrass]] and lay [[turtle eggs]]. They are the only source of [[turtle scute]]s, which drop from baby turtles when they mature into adults, and can be used to craft [[Turtle Shell|turtle shell]] helmets.

== Spawning ==
Turtles occasionally spawn in small groups on the sand in [[beach]]es, but not in [[snowy beach]]es or [[stony shore]]s.

Turtles have a 5% chance to spawn as babies.

{{IN|Java}}, turtles spawn in groups of up to 5 individuals, y level less than 4 blocks above [[sea level]] (from y level -64 to 66, inclusive), and on blocks with the [[Block_tag_(Java_Edition)#sand|sand]] tag (sand, red sand, and suspicious sand).

{{IN|bedrock}}, turtles spawn in groups of 2–6, at Y=60–67.

{{Mob spawn table}}

== Drops ==
=== Breeding ===
Upon successful [[breeding]], {{xp|1|7}} is dropped.
=== On death ===
{{DropTable
