lightning = Only when killed by [[lightning]]. {{IN|je}}, the tick after the turtle has been killed, the items get destroyed by the lightning bolt if they are within 3 blocks.
}}
* {{xp|1|3}}, if killed by a [[player]] or tamed [[wolf]].

Baby turtles do not drop anything when they [[die]].

=== Growth ===
When a baby turtle matures into an adult, it drops 1 {{ItemLink|turtle scute}}.

== Behavior ==
[[File:Turtle swimming.png|thumb|A turtle swimming.]]
Turtles can move around slowly on land and swim at a fast speed in [[water]]. Like other passive mobs, they move around aimlessly and flee when attacked. When on land, they generally attempt to move to the nearest water source that is at least 2 blocks deep, regardless if player made or natural. When in an enclosed area, such as a player-made enclosure, they generally swim in circles if the water is in the area, and rarely go on land to explore, if there is any.

Turtles cannot be attached to [[lead]]s,<ref>{{bug|MC-125629||Turtles can't be leashed|WAI}}</ref> but they can be led by a [[player]] holding [[seagrass]] within 10 blocks of the turtle.

Turtles can be picked up by [[boat]]s and [[minecart]]s.

Turtles are dealt 3.4×10<sup>38</sup> ({{healthbar|2|9px}} × 1.7×10<sup>38</sup>){{only|je|short=1}}/{{hp|10000}}{{only|be|short=1}} damage when struck by lightning.

As with other [[aquatic mobs]], turtles suffer extra damage when hit by a [[trident]] with the [[Impaling]] enchantment {{in|java}}, and cannot drown, despite the fact that real-life turtles breathe air.

